// ============================================================================
//  Futures Compounding Machine
//  Gann Swing Lanes signal engine with small-account compounding risk controls
//  Pine Script v6
//
//  OVERVIEW:
//    Same Gann swing signal logic as GannSwingLanes_TradersPost.pine, with
//    additional risk/compounding controls for disciplined small-account growth.
//    Designed primarily for MYM and MES.
//
//  COMPOUNDING CONTROLS:
//    1. Max Daily Loss         — cumulative intraday loss halts all new entries
//                               for the remainder of the day. Resets each morning.
//    2. Max Consecutive Losses — N losses in a row halts trading for the day.
//    3. Trade Profit Target    — dollar-based take-profit converted to a limit
//                               price via the instrument tick value. Warning label
//                               appears when the target falls below one tick.
//    4. Compound Ratio         — win: target x ratio. Loss: target / ratio.
//                               Grows winners over time, shrinks after losses.
//                               Floor is always one tick.
//
//  RISK:REWARD GATE:
//    Before each entry, the TP distance is compared against the stop distance
//    (pivot to entry, or 1x ATR when no pivot stop is set). Entries are skipped
//    when the R:R falls below the minimum threshold.
//
//  TIME-OF-DAY WINDOWS:
//    Four CT time windows each have an enable toggle and their own compound ratio.
//    Disable a window to block all entries during that period. The compound ratio
//    applied on a trade's close is the one captured at entry time, so a trade
//    entered in the morning keeps the morning ratio regardless of when it closes.
//    The fallback ratio (GRP_COMP) is used when no window is active (off-hours).
//
//  DIFFERENCE FROM BASE STRATEGY:
//    The base strategy exits on the next opposing swing signal (full swing run).
//    This strategy exits at a fixed dollar TP limit — smaller, more consistent
//    wins designed to compound a small account without large drawdowns.
//
//  INSTRUMENT AUTO-CONFIG:
//    All 6 calibrated micro-futures configs are retained (MYM, MES, MNQ,
//    M2K, MGC, MBT). MYM and MES are the primary focus instruments.
//
//  NOTE ON "BOTH" MODE REVERSAL TIMING:
//    When a reversal fires (e.g., short closes and long opens on the same bar),
//    compound/halt state updates one bar later due to Pine Script bar-close
//    order sequencing. The TP limit self-corrects the following bar.
//
//  CHANGELOG:
//    v4 — Jun 2026 (cash-open blackout):
//      1. New "Block Entries Around Cash Open" gate (GRP_SES). Blocks NEW entries
//         inside a configurable window (default 08:25–08:35 CT, inclusive) around
//         the 08:30 CT / 09:30 ET equity-index cash open. Rationale: a swing entry
//         taken into the open bar can have its hard stop gapped straight through —
//         a tight MYM stop ($10/20 pts under Auto-Config) filled ~$77 on a single
//         150-pt open bar, blowing past Max Loss Per Trade. Blocking entry in the
//         window avoids initiating into that gap; open positions/stops unaffected.
//         Status label shows [OPEN BLACKOUT] while active.
//    v3 — Jun 2026 (RSI confirmation gate):
//      1. Entry second-confirmation: a Gann swing signal alone no longer fires an
//         entry — RSI must also be *sharply* trending in the trade direction.
//         "Sharp" = RSI slope (rsi − rsi[slopeLen]) beyond a threshold; longs need
//         sharp-up, shorts sharp-down. Optional midline gate also requires RSI on
//         the bullish/bearish side of 50. Toggle: "Require RSI Entry Confirmation".
//      2. Exit on RSI reversal (OR with TP / stop / EOD): while in a position, if
//         the RSI slope flips against the trade beyond the exit threshold the
//         position is closed at market ("RSI Reversal"). Routes through the normal
//         trade-close path → compounding update + {"action":"exit"} alert fire as
//         usual. Toggle: "Exit on RSI Reversal".
//      3. RSI inputs live in their own "RSI Confirmation" group as global filters
//         (not yet per-instrument auto-configured — calibrate, then promote into
//         InstrumentConfig later, same as the MGC/MBT placeholder pattern). RSI
//         value + slope are shown in the status label (no chart plot — overlay pane).
//    v2 — Jun 2026 (live validation review):
//      1. calc_on_every_tick remains false: tick-by-tick eval was tested but caused
//         immediate exits on MYM — $10 hard stop (20 pts) fires on normal intrabar
//         noise. Native NT bracket stop via stopPrice in alert handles tick-level
//         protection instead; TV simulation stays bar-close only.
//      2. Stop price in entry alerts: entry JSON now includes "stopPrice" so
//         TradersPost can place a native bracket stop in NinjaTrader at fill time.
//         NinjaTrader no longer depends solely on TradingView webhook delivery to
//         protect the position.
//      3. Pre-market hard floor: entries blocked before PRE_MARKET_FLOOR (07:00 CT)
//         regardless of sessionStartHr input. Orange warning label fires when the
//         chart is in pre-market hours.
//      4. MYM sizing ladder slowed: sizeUpEvery $50→$100, sizeDownEvery $50→$75.
//         Reached 4 contracts in 3 days at $50 — too aggressive for live validation.
//      5. MES pivot stop enabled: gives MES a structural stop level for the broker
//         bracket order rather than relying solely on the R:R gate.
// ============================================================================

//@version=6
strategy("Futures Compounding Machine",
         overlay            = true,
         default_qty_type   = strategy.fixed,
         default_qty_value  = 1,
         pyramiding         = 0,
         calc_on_every_tick = false)

// ── User-Defined Types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

type SwingState
    bool  lastWasUp = false
    bool  lastWasDn = false
    float upHigh    = na
    int   upBar     = na
    float downLow   = na
    int   downBar   = na

type PivotPoints
    chart.point high = na
    chart.point low  = na

type InstrumentConfig
    // ── Signal Filters ─────────────────────────────────
    bool  pivotStop   = false               // Enable Pivot Stop
    float swingSize   = 1.6                 // Min Swing Size (x ATR)
    int   cooldown    = 3                   // Cooldown (bars)
    int   emaLen      = 20                  // Trend EMA Length (reference — effEmaLen uses cfgEmaLen switch)
    bool  breakeven   = false               // Enable Auto Breakeven
    // ── Risk Management ────────────────────────────────
    float pivotBuf    = 0.25               // Pivot Buffer (x ATR)
    float beTrigger   = 2.0                // Breakeven Trigger (x ATR)
    float beBuf       = 0.5                // Breakeven Buffer (x ATR)
    bool  rrGate      = false              // Enable R:R Gate
    float rrMinVal    = 1.5                // Min Reward:Risk Ratio
    // ── Compounding Controls ───────────────────────────
    bool  resetTp     = false              // Reset TP Target Each Day
    float initTp      = 35.0              // Initial Trade Profit Target ($)
    float maxDaily    = 35.0              // Max Daily Loss ($)
    int   maxConsec   = 3                 // Max Consecutive Losses
    float maxLoss     = 70.0              // Max Loss Per Trade ($)
    float fallRatio   = 1.1               // Fallback Compound Ratio
    // ── Time Windows ───────────────────────────────────
    bool  w1En        = true              // Enable Morning 07-11 CT
    float w1Ratio     = 1.15             // Morning Compound Ratio
    bool  w2En        = false             // Enable Midday 11-13 CT
    float w2Ratio     = 1.0              // Midday Compound Ratio
    bool  w3En        = true              // Enable Afternoon 13-16 CT
    float w3Ratio     = 1.05             // Afternoon Compound Ratio
    bool  w4En        = false             // Enable Late Day 16-17 CT
    float w4Ratio     = 1.0              // Late Day Compound Ratio
    // ── Day Bias ───────────────────────────────────────
    bool   useApex    = false             // Use Embedded Apex Trend Signal
    string apexMode   = "Trend (Adaptive MA)"  // Apex Signal Mode
    int    apexPeriod = 20               // Apex Lookback Period (reference — use cfgApexPeriod for ta.*)
    string apexTf     = "D"              // Apex Signal Timeframe (reference — use cfgApexTf for request.*)
    // ── Day Bias Control ───────────────────────────────
    bool  neutralBias   = true            // Neutral Bias allows both directions (false = block all when neutral)
    // ── Position Sizing ────────────────────────────────
    bool  autoSize      = false           // Per-instrument sizing enable
    float sizeUpEvery   = 50.0           // Add 1 contract per $X cumul profit (default conservative = MYM)
    float sizeDownEvery = 50.0           // Remove 1 contract per $Y drawdown (default conservative = MYM)
    int   sizeMax       = 3              // Max additional contracts (default conservative = MYM)

// ── Per-Instrument Config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Calibrated for 0700-1700 CT session (Oct 2025 - May 2026, 5-min bars).
// Pattern: InstrumentConfig.new() uses UDT defaults (= fallback).
//          Only fields that differ from the defaults are explicitly set.
getConfig(string root) =>
    InstrumentConfig cfg = InstrumentConfig.new()
    if root == "MYM"
        // Signal Filters
        cfg.swingSize  := 2.1
        cfg.cooldown   := 6
        cfg.emaLen     := 17
        // Risk Management
        cfg.breakeven  := true
        cfg.pivotBuf   := 0.35
        cfg.beTrigger  := 1.7
        cfg.beBuf      := 1.19
        // Compounding
        cfg.resetTp    := true
        cfg.initTp     := 30.0
        cfg.maxDaily   := 30.0
        cfg.maxConsec  := 4
        cfg.maxLoss    := 10.0
        cfg.fallRatio  := 1.2
        // Time Windows
        cfg.w1Ratio    := 1.35
        cfg.w2Ratio    := 1.25
        cfg.w3Ratio    := 1.25
        cfg.w4En       := true
        cfg.w4Ratio    := 1.2
        // Day Bias
        cfg.useApex    := true
        cfg.apexMode   := "Structure (BOS/CHoCH)"
        cfg.apexPeriod := 9
        cfg.apexTf     := "120"
        // Position Sizing — slowed Jun 2026: $100 up / $75 down / max+3.
        // Was $50/$50 (UDT defaults) — reached 4 contracts in 3 live days.
        // Conservative until stop architecture confirmed reliable.
        cfg.autoSize      := true
        cfg.sizeUpEvery   := 100.0
        cfg.sizeDownEvery := 75.0
    else if root == "MES"
        // Signal Filters
        cfg.swingSize  := 2.1
        cfg.cooldown   := 4
        cfg.emaLen     := 18
        // Risk Management — breakeven intentionally OFF (BE stops kill TP compounding on MES)
        // pivotStop enabled Jun 2026: provides structural stop level for broker bracket order.
        cfg.pivotStop  := true
        cfg.rrGate     := true
        // Compounding
        cfg.resetTp    := true
        cfg.maxConsec  := 2
        cfg.fallRatio  := 1.2
        // Day Bias — Apex ON, neutral blocks entries (don't trade when direction unclear)
        cfg.useApex    := true
        cfg.apexMode   := "Structure (BOS/CHoCH)"
        cfg.apexPeriod := 8
        cfg.neutralBias := false
        // apexTf stays "D" (UDT default)
        // Position Sizing — validated Oct 2025–May 2026: $200/$150/max+5
        cfg.autoSize      := true
        cfg.sizeUpEvery   := 200.0
        cfg.sizeDownEvery := 150.0
        cfg.sizeMax       := 5
    else if root == "MNQ"
        cfg.emaLen     := 11
        cfg.resetTp    := true
        // NQ ATR-based stop ~$128 (swingSize 1.6 × ~$80 MNQ ATR); TP must be 1.5x = $192+
        cfg.initTp     := 200.0
        // maxLoss caps individual risk; structural stops can be $200+; capped at $100 gives 2:1 R:R
        cfg.maxLoss    := 100.0
        cfg.rrGate     := true
        // Sizing: $200/$150/max+2 — capped at 3c total; 4c tier had 33% win + gap-through risk ($970 worst)
        cfg.autoSize      := true
        cfg.sizeUpEvery   := 200.0
        cfg.sizeDownEvery := 150.0
        cfg.sizeMax       := 2
    else if root == "M2K"
        cfg.swingSize  := 2.1
        cfg.emaLen     := 8
        // Critical: resetTp=false causes TP to compound to unusable levels (same bug as MES)
        cfg.resetTp    := true
        cfg.rrGate     := true
        // Sizing: $200/$150/max+3 matches MES risk profile (same $70/contract stop)
        // $50 threshold (MYM default) scales after 1–2 trades — too aggressive for M2K's volatility
        cfg.autoSize      := true
        cfg.sizeUpEvery   := 200.0
        cfg.sizeDownEvery := 150.0
        cfg.sizeMax       := 3
    else if root == "MGC"
        cfg.swingSize  := 2.1
        cfg.cooldown   := 6
        cfg.emaLen     := 7
        cfg.resetTp    := true
        // pivotStop removed: pivot stops > $35 TP → failed rrGate → zero trades
        // rrGate removed: gold ATR × 2.1 swingSize also exceeds $35 TP at 1.5× threshold
        // Sizing: $200/$150/max+3 — placeholder; calibrate when ready
        cfg.autoSize      := true
        cfg.sizeUpEvery   := 200.0
        cfg.sizeDownEvery := 150.0
        cfg.sizeMax       := 3
    else if root == "MBT"
        cfg.swingSize  := 5.0
        cfg.cooldown   := 6
        cfg.emaLen     := 8
        cfg.resetTp    := true
        // initTp raised $35→$100: at $35 TP vs $70 stop R:R=0.5 → −EV even at 61% win; $100 gives 1.43:1
        cfg.initTp     := 100.0
        // Sizing: $500/$300/max+2 — conservative given BTC per-trade dollar swings
        cfg.autoSize      := true
        cfg.sizeUpEvery   := 500.0
        cfg.sizeDownEvery := 300.0
        cfg.sizeMax       := 2
    cfg

// ── Input Groups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string GRP_AUTO = "Instrument Auto-Config"
var string GRP_COMP = "Compounding & Risk Controls"
var string GRP_TOD  = "Time-of-Day Windows (America/Chicago)"
var string GRP_SIG  = "Signal Settings"
var string GRP_BIAS = "Day Bias (Direction Override)"
var string GRP_SIZE = "Position Sizing"
var string GRP_RISK = "Risk Management"
var string GRP_FILT = "Signal Filters"
var string GRP_RSI  = "RSI Confirmation (Entry + Exit)"
var string GRP_SES  = "Session & Hours (CME Futures)"
var string GRP_EXEC = "Order Execution (TradersPost)"
var string GRP_VIS  = "Visuals"

// ── Auto-Config ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool autoConfig = input.bool(true, "Auto-Configure by Instrument",
    tooltip = "Applies calibrated settings for MYM, MES, MNQ, M2K, MGC, MBT. Manual filter inputs below are overridden.",
    group   = GRP_AUTO)

int contracts = input.int(1, "Contracts per Trade",
    minval  = 1,
    tooltip = "Start at 1 contract. Scale up only after consistent live profitability at this level.",
    group   = GRP_SIZE)

bool  useAutoSize  = input.bool(true, "Enable Auto Position Sizing",
    tooltip = "Scales contracts based on cumulative P&L growth and drawdown. The Scale Up/Down thresholds and Max Additional Contracts below are always live — change them and the backtest updates immediately. When Auto-Configure is ON, the per-instrument config determines whether sizing is active for that instrument (currently ON for MES, OFF for others); uncheck this box to disable sizing entirely regardless of auto-config.",
    group   = GRP_SIZE)
float sizeUpEvery  = input.float(50.0, "Scale Up Every ($)  [auto-config OFF only]",
    minval  = 10.0, step = 10.0,
    tooltip = "Used only when Auto-Configure is OFF. Add 1 contract per $X cumulative profit. When Auto-Configure is ON, calibrated per-instrument values are used instead: MYM $50, MES $200.",
    group   = GRP_SIZE)
float sizeDnEvery  = input.float(50.0, "Scale Down Every ($)  [auto-config OFF only]",
    minval  = 10.0, step = 10.0,
    tooltip = "Used only when Auto-Configure is OFF. Remove 1 contract per $Y drawdown from peak. When Auto-Configure is ON, calibrated per-instrument values are used instead: MYM $50, MES $150.",
    group   = GRP_SIZE)
int   sizeMax      = input.int(3, "Max Additional Contracts  [auto-config OFF only]",
    minval  = 1, maxval = 20,
    tooltip = "Used only when Auto-Configure is OFF. Hard cap on extra contracts above base. When Auto-Configure is ON, calibrated per-instrument values are used instead: MYM 3, MES 5.",
    group   = GRP_SIZE)

string tradeDir = input.string("Both", "Trade Direction",
    options = ["Both", "Long Only", "Short Only"],
    tooltip = "Default direction when no Day Bias is active.",
    group   = GRP_SIG)

// ── Day Bias (Direction Override) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two modes — only one is active at a time, Apex wins when enabled:
//
//   MANUAL  — type any text each morning; fuzzy-matched for "bull"/"bear".
//             Leave blank to fall back to the Trade Direction setting above.
//
//   APEX    — embeds the Apex Adaptive Trend Navigator algorithm directly;
//             no external indicator required. Reads from any symbol you choose
//             (e.g. SPY for MES, DIA for MYM) for market-level sentiment.

string manualBiasText = input.string("", "Manual Day Bias  (type bull / bear / neutral / both / blank)",
    tooltip  = "Fuzzy text match — any word containing 'bull' = long only, 'bear' = short only, 'neutral' or 'both' = both directions. Leave blank to use the Trade Direction setting. Case-insensitive. Example: 'bullish day', 'BEARISH open', 'neutral watch'.",
    group    = GRP_BIAS)

bool neutralTrades = input.bool(true, "Neutral Bias = Allow Both Directions",
    tooltip  = "ON (default): when bias is Neutral or unset, both longs and shorts are allowed as normal. OFF: a Neutral bias blocks all new entries — use when you want to sit out unclear days entirely.",
    group    = GRP_BIAS)

bool useApexBias = input.bool(false, "Use Embedded Apex Trend Signal  (overrides Manual)",
    tooltip  = "Activates the built-in Apex Adaptive Trend Navigator. Computes on the Trend Reference Symbol below. Overrides the Manual Day Bias. Adapted from Apex Adaptive Trend Navigator [Pineify], MPL 2.0.",
    group    = GRP_BIAS)

string apexSymbolInput = input.symbol("", "  Trend Reference Symbol  (blank = current chart)",
    tooltip  = "Symbol whose price drives the Apex trend signal. Blank = current chart instrument. For equity index futures: SPY or XSP (MES), DIA (MYM), QQQ or NDX (MNQ), IWM (M2K). For gold: GC1! For BTC: BTCUSDT or INDEX:BTCUSD.",
    group    = GRP_BIAS)

string apexModeInput = input.string("Trend (Adaptive MA)", "  Apex Signal Mode",
    options  = ["Trend (Adaptive MA)", "Structure (BOS/CHoCH)", "Both Agree"],
    tooltip  = "Trend: price vs adaptive MA — fast and reactive. Structure: Break-of-Structure via higher highs / lower lows — slower, more structural. Both Agree: only directional when MA trend and structure point the same way; Neutral otherwise.",
    group    = GRP_BIAS)

int apexLen = input.int(20, "  Apex Lookback Period",
    minval   = 5,
    tooltip  = "Bars used for efficiency calculation and pivot detection. Default 20 matches the original Apex indicator.",
    group    = GRP_BIAS)

string apexTimeframe = input.timeframe("D", "  Apex Signal Timeframe",
    tooltip  = "Timeframe used for Apex trend calculations. 'D' (Daily, default) means the bias is derived from the previous confirmed daily close and stays constant all day — best for backtesting as a proxy for your morning directional read. Use the chart timeframe (leave blank or match your chart) for an intraday trend filter that updates every bar.",
    group    = GRP_BIAS)

// ── Compounding & Risk Controls ───────────────────────────────────────────────
float maxDailyLoss = input.float(35.0, "Max Daily Loss ($)",
    minval  = 1.0, step = 5.0,
    tooltip = "Hard trading stop for the day once cumulative intraday losses reach this amount. Resets each morning. Increase gradually as the account grows.",
    group   = GRP_COMP)

int maxConsecLosses = input.int(3, "Max Consecutive Losses",
    minval  = 1,
    tooltip = "Trading halts for the day the moment this many losses occur back-to-back, regardless of total dollar loss.",
    group   = GRP_COMP)

int maxConsecDays = input.int(2, "Max Consecutive Loss Days",
    minval  = 1,
    tooltip = "Blocks all new entries on a day if this many consecutive calendar days have each ended with a net loss. A profitable day resets the counter. Example: 2 = after 2 back-to-back losing days, trading is skipped the next day. Provides a circuit-breaker during sustained adverse market conditions.",
    group   = GRP_COMP)

float initTradeProfit = input.float(35.0, "Initial Trade Profit Target ($)",
    minval  = 1.0, step = 5.0,
    tooltip = "Starting dollar take-profit per trade. Converted to a limit price via the instrument's tick value. A warning label appears if the target falls below one tick.",
    group   = GRP_COMP)

float compoundRatio = input.float(1.1, "Fallback Compound Ratio",
    minval  = 1.0, step = 0.05,
    tooltip = "Used when no Time-of-Day window is active (off-hours or all windows disabled). Also the default when time-of-day windows are all OFF. Set 1.0 to disable compounding.",
    group   = GRP_COMP)

bool resetTpDaily = input.bool(false, "Reset TP Target Each Day",
    tooltip = "ON: compound profit target resets to Initial Trade Profit Target each morning. OFF: compounded value carries forward across sessions.",
    group   = GRP_COMP)

float maxLossPerTrade = input.float(70.0, "Max Loss Per Trade ($)",
    minval  = 1.0, step = 5.0,
    tooltip = "Hard dollar stop always active on every trade, regardless of pivot stop or breakeven settings. Prevents any single trade losing more than this amount. Default 70 = 2× a $35 TP target. Adjust proportionally when TP changes.",
    group   = GRP_COMP)

float minTpPct = input.float(40.0, "Minimum TP Floor (% of Initial Target)",
    minval  = 10.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 5.0,
    tooltip = "Entries pause when the compounded TP falls below this percentage of the Initial Trade Profit Target. Prevents trading at unfavourable R:R after a loss run. Example: 40% of $35 initial = $14 floor. Scales automatically across instruments and initial target sizes. Entries resume once wins compound the TP back above the floor.",
    group   = GRP_COMP)

// ── Time-of-Day Windows ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Each window has an enable toggle and its own compound ratio.
// When a window is disabled no entries fire during that period.
// The ratio captured at entry is applied on trade close regardless of exit time.

bool  useWin1  = input.bool(true,  "Enable Morning   07:00 - 11:00 CT",
    tooltip = "Cleanest directional moves of the day. Institutional position-building hour.",
    group   = GRP_TOD)
float win1Ratio = input.float(1.15, "  Morning Compound Ratio",
    minval  = 1.0, step = 0.05,
    tooltip = "Higher ratio rewards the stronger morning trend bias. Applied to win/loss compounding for trades entered in this window.",
    group   = GRP_TOD)

bool  useWin2  = input.bool(false, "Enable Midday    11:00 - 13:00 CT",
    tooltip = "Lunch-hour chop — often the weakest signal quality of the day. Disabled by default.",
    group   = GRP_TOD)
float win2Ratio = input.float(1.0,  "  Midday Compound Ratio",
    minval  = 1.0, step = 0.05,
    tooltip = "Set to 1.0 (no compounding) by default — midday signals are lower confidence.",
    group   = GRP_TOD)

bool  useWin3  = input.bool(true,  "Enable Afternoon 13:00 - 16:00 CT",
    tooltip = "Post-lunch trend continuation or late-day momentum. Generally better than midday.",
    group   = GRP_TOD)
float win3Ratio = input.float(1.05, "  Afternoon Compound Ratio",
    minval  = 1.0, step = 0.05,
    tooltip = "Moderate ratio — afternoon moves are real but shorter than morning.",
    group   = GRP_TOD)

bool  useWin4  = input.bool(false, "Enable Late Day  16:00 - 17:00 CT",
    tooltip = "Final hour before EOD close. Thin liquidity and erratic moves. Disabled by default.",
    group   = GRP_TOD)
float win4Ratio = input.float(1.0,  "  Late Day Compound Ratio",
    minval  = 1.0, step = 0.05,
    tooltip = "Set to 1.0 (no compounding) — late-day signals are lowest confidence.",
    group   = GRP_TOD)

// ── Risk Management ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool  useStopLoss   = input.bool(true,  "Enable Pivot Stop",
    tooltip = "Stop just beyond the swing pivot — the natural Gann invalidation level. [Overridden when Auto-Config is ON]",
    group   = GRP_RISK)
float pivotBuffer   = input.float(0.25, "Pivot Buffer (x ATR)",
    minval  = 0.0, step = 0.05,
    tooltip = "ATR cushion past the pivot to avoid exact-level stop-outs.",
    group   = GRP_RISK)
bool  useBreakeven  = input.bool(false, "Enable Auto Breakeven",
    tooltip = "Once the trade moves N x ATR in your favor the stop shifts to entry + buffer. [Overridden when Auto-Config is ON]",
    group   = GRP_RISK)
float beTriggerMult = input.float(2.0,  "Breakeven Trigger (x ATR)",
    minval  = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = GRP_RISK)
float beBuffer      = input.float(0.5,  "Breakeven Buffer (x ATR)",
    minval  = 0.0, step = 0.25, group = GRP_RISK)
float beFloorDollars = input.float(15.0, "Breakeven Dollar Floor ($)",
    minval  = 0.0, step = 5.0,
    tooltip = "BE also triggers when favorable excursion reaches this dollar amount, regardless of ATR multiple. Acts as a safety net in high-volatility markets where ATR is large and the ATR-based trigger fires too late. Set 0 to disable. Default $15 = trigger BE once the trade is $15 in your favour.",
    group   = GRP_RISK)

bool  useRRGate = input.bool(true, "Enable R:R Gate",
    tooltip = "Blocks entries where the reward (TP distance) divided by the risk (stop distance) falls below the minimum. When Pivot Stop is OFF, 1x ATR is used as the implied risk.",
    group   = GRP_RISK)
float rrMin     = input.float(1.5, "Min Reward:Risk Ratio",
    minval  = 0.5, step = 0.25,
    tooltip = "1.5 means the TP target must be at least 1.5x the stop distance. Raise to 2.0 for higher-quality entries only.",
    group   = GRP_RISK)

// ── Signal Filters ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool  useTrendFilter = input.bool(true,  "Enable Trend Filter",
    tooltip = "Long signals only above the EMA; short signals only below it.",
    group   = GRP_FILT)
int   trendLen       = input.int(20,     "Trend EMA Length",
    minval  = 5,
    tooltip = "[Overridden when Auto-Config is ON]",
    group   = GRP_FILT)
bool  useSwingSize   = input.bool(true,  "Enable Minimum Swing Size",
    tooltip = "Swing leg must be at least N x ATR. Filters micro choppy flips.",
    group   = GRP_FILT)
float atrMult        = input.float(1.8,  "Min Swing Size (x ATR)",
    minval  = 0.1, step = 0.1,
    tooltip = "[Overridden when Auto-Config is ON]",
    group   = GRP_FILT)
bool  useCooldown    = input.bool(true,  "Enable Cooldown",
    tooltip = "Blocks re-entry for N bars after any trade closes.",
    group   = GRP_FILT)
int   cooldownBars   = input.int(4,      "Cooldown (bars)",
    minval  = 1,
    tooltip = "[Overridden when Auto-Config is ON]",
    group   = GRP_FILT)

// ── RSI Confirmation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Second confirmation on top of the Gann swing signal. A swing alone is no longer
// enough — RSI momentum must agree with the trade direction at entry, and an
// optional RSI reversal closes the position early (OR with the TP / stop / EOD).
// These are GLOBAL filters (not per-instrument auto-config). Calibrate per symbol
// with Auto-Config OFF first, then promote into InstrumentConfig if desired.
bool  useRsiEntry  = input.bool(true,  "Require RSI Entry Confirmation",
    tooltip = "ON: a long needs RSI sharply UP-trending, a short needs RSI sharply DOWN-trending, in addition to the swing signal. OFF: RSI is ignored at entry.",
    group   = GRP_RSI)
int   rsiLen       = input.int(14,     "RSI Length",
    minval  = 2,
    tooltip = "Lookback for the RSI itself. 14 = standard.",
    group   = GRP_RSI)
int   rsiSlopeLen  = input.int(3,      "RSI Slope Lookback (bars)",
    minval  = 1,
    tooltip = "'Sharp' is measured as the RSI change over this many bars: slope = rsi − rsi[N]. Smaller = more reactive / sharper requirement window.",
    group   = GRP_RSI)
float rsiEntrySlope = input.float(3.0, "Min Entry Slope (RSI pts over lookback)",
    minval  = 0.0, step = 0.5,
    tooltip = "Minimum RSI rise (long) or fall (short) over the slope lookback to confirm an entry. Higher = only steeper momentum qualifies. Example: 3.0 over 3 bars.",
    group   = GRP_RSI)
bool  useRsiMid    = input.bool(true,  "Also Require RSI Above/Below Midline",
    tooltip = "ON: longs additionally require RSI above the midline, shorts below it — RSI must be sharply trending AND on the correct side of 50.",
    group   = GRP_RSI)
float rsiMidLevel  = input.float(50.0, "  RSI Midline",
    minval  = 1.0, maxval = 99.0, step = 1.0,
    tooltip = "Midline for the optional side gate. 50 = neutral RSI. Raise/lower to demand stronger momentum before entry.",
    group   = GRP_RSI)
bool  useRsiExit   = input.bool(true,  "Exit on RSI Reversal",
    tooltip = "ON: while in a trade, if RSI slope flips against the position beyond the exit threshold below, close at market ('RSI Reversal'). This is an OR with the TP, stop, and EOD exits — whichever triggers first wins.",
    group   = GRP_RSI)
float rsiExitSlope = input.float(3.0, "  Min Reversal Slope (RSI pts over lookback)",
    minval  = 0.5, step = 0.5,
    tooltip = "How sharply RSI must move AGAINST the position (over the slope lookback) to trigger an early exit. For a long: RSI falling this many points. For a short: RSI rising this many points.",
    group   = GRP_RSI)

// ── Session ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// NOTE: input.session() with a TZ override silently fails on 24h continuous
// futures contracts in TradingView — session strings are not reliable for
// overnight Globex data. Direct hour()/minute() comparisons are used instead.
// All times are America/Chicago (CT).
// IMPORTANT — CME equity index futures (MYM, MES, MNQ, M2K) halt from
// 16:00–16:30 CT daily.  Default times below keep all activity before that
// window.  If you trade MGC (gold halts 17:00–18:00 CT) or MBT (24/7) you
// can push these later.  Watchlist alerts do not fire during maintenance halts
// regardless of what the strategy logic requests.
int  sessionStartHr = input.int(7,  "Session Start Hour (CT, 24h)",
    minval  = 0, maxval = 23,
    tooltip = "Entries allowed from this CT hour onward. Default 7 = 07:00 CT.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
int  sessionEndHr   = input.int(16, "Session End Hour (CT, 24h)",
    minval  = 0, maxval = 23,
    tooltip = "Absolute session end — used only for the inSession flag, not for EOD close timing.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
int  sessionOpenBuffer = input.int(2, "Session Open Buffer (bars)",
    minval  = 0, maxval = 20,
    tooltip = "Skip this many bars after session start before allowing entries. Prevents acting on swing state built during pre-market. Default 2 = 10 minutes on a 5-min chart.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
int  entryLockHr    = input.int(15, "Lock New Entries After Hour (CT)",
    minval  = 0, maxval = 23,
    tooltip = "No new entries at or after this hour + minute. Default 15 keeps the lock well before the 16:00 CT maintenance halt.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
int  entryLockMin   = input.int(30, "Lock New Entries After Minute",
    minval  = 0, maxval = 59,
    tooltip = "Combined with Lock Hour — no new entries after HH:MM CT. Default 15:30 CT.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
// ── Cash-Open Blackout ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Blocks NEW entries around the 08:30 CT (09:30 ET) equity-index cash open, the
// most gap-prone minutes of the day. A swing entry taken into that bar can have
// its hard stop gapped straight through (e.g. a $10/20-pt MYM stop filling ~$77
// when the open bar travels 150 pts). Blocking entry in the window avoids
// initiating into that gap. Exits/stops on already-open positions are unaffected.
bool useOpenBlackout = input.bool(true, "Block Entries Around Cash Open",
    tooltip = "ON: no new entries inside the blackout window below (defaults to the 08:30 CT cash open ±5 min). Existing positions and their stops are unaffected. Targets the gap-through that makes a single open-bar loss exceed Max Loss Per Trade.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
int  openBlackoutStartHr  = input.int(8,  "  Blackout Start Hour (CT)",
    minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = GRP_SES)
int  openBlackoutStartMin = input.int(25, "  Blackout Start Minute",
    minval = 0, maxval = 59, group = GRP_SES)
int  openBlackoutEndHr    = input.int(8,  "  Blackout End Hour (CT)",
    minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = GRP_SES)
int  openBlackoutEndMin   = input.int(35, "  Blackout End Minute",
    minval = 0, maxval = 59,
    tooltip = "Blackout is inclusive of start and end minute. Default 08:25–08:35 CT covers the 08:30 cash-open spike. Widen (e.g. to 08:40) if gaps persist into the first 10 minutes.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
int  eodCloseHr     = input.int(15, "EOD Force-Close Hour (CT)",
    minval  = 0, maxval = 23,
    tooltip = "Force-close fires at eodCloseHr:eodCloseMin CT. Default 15 (3pm). Must be before 16:00 CT for equity index futures to avoid the maintenance halt.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
int  eodMinute      = input.int(45, "EOD Force-Close Minute (CT)",
    minval  = 0, maxval = 59,
    tooltip = "Combined with EOD Hour. Default 45 = 15:45 CT — ahead of broker auto-liquidation at 3:45 CT. Also clears before the 16:00 CME maintenance halt.",
    group   = GRP_SES)
var string TZ = "America/Chicago"

// PRE_MARKET_FLOOR: hard minimum hour (CT) below which entries are always blocked,
// regardless of sessionStartHr. Protects against thin pre-market liquidity and
// NinjaTrader session misconfiguration where NT runs with different hours than TV.
// Cannot be lowered via inputs. 07:00 CT = 08:00 ET (1h before US open).
int PRE_MARKET_FLOOR = 7

// ── Order Execution ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool useMarketOrders = input.bool(true, "Use Market Orders",
    tooltip = "ON = no price field sent, TradersPost submits a market order (recommended). OFF = limit at close +/- pad ticks.",
    group   = GRP_EXEC)
int padTicks = input.int(4, "Entry Pad (ticks, limit mode only)",
    minval  = 1, maxval = 50,
    tooltip = "Only used when Market Orders is OFF.",
    group   = GRP_EXEC)

// ── Visuals ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool  drawArrows  = input.bool(true,          "Draw Arrows",              group = GRP_VIS)
bool  drawLines   = input.bool(true,          "Draw Swing Lines",         group = GRP_VIS)
bool  drawEma     = input.bool(true,          "Draw Trend EMA",           group = GRP_VIS)
bool  showStatus  = input.bool(true,          "Show Status Label",        group = GRP_VIS)
color upColor     = input.color(color.lime,   "Buy Arrow Color",          group = GRP_VIS)
color dnColor     = input.color(color.red,    "Sell Arrow Color",         group = GRP_VIS)
color lineColor   = input.color(color.yellow, "Swing Line Color",         group = GRP_VIS)
color emaColor    = input.color(color.aqua,   "Trend EMA Color",          group = GRP_VIS)
int   lineWt      = input.int(2, "Line Weight", minval = 1, maxval = 5,   group = GRP_VIS)

// ── Resolve Effective Signal Parameters ───────────────────────────────────────
InstrumentConfig cfg = getConfig(syminfo.root)

bool  effPivotStop = autoConfig ? cfg.pivotStop : useStopLoss
float effSwingSize = autoConfig ? cfg.swingSize : atrMult
int   effCooldown  = autoConfig ? cfg.cooldown  : cooldownBars
bool  effBreakeven = autoConfig ? cfg.breakeven : useBreakeven

// ta.ema, ta.pivothigh, ta.pivotlow, and request.security timeframe all require
// simple int / simple string.  Switch expressions with literal arms return simple
// values — struct field access does not, hence these parallel switch statements.
int cfgEmaLen = switch syminfo.root
    "MYM" => 17
    "MES" => 18
    "MNQ" => 11
    "M2K" =>  8
    "MGC" =>  7
    "MBT" =>  8
    => 20
int effEmaLen = autoConfig ? cfgEmaLen : trendLen

int cfgApexPeriod = switch syminfo.root
    "MYM" => 9
    "MES" => 8
    => 20
int effApexPeriod = autoConfig ? cfgApexPeriod : apexLen

string cfgApexTf = switch syminfo.root
    "MYM" => "120"
    => "D"
string effApexTfInput = autoConfig ? cfgApexTf : apexTimeframe

// ── Resolved Risk Management ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
float effPivotBuf   = autoConfig ? cfg.pivotBuf   : pivotBuffer
float effBeTrigger  = autoConfig ? cfg.beTrigger  : beTriggerMult
float effBeBuf      = autoConfig ? cfg.beBuf      : beBuffer
bool  effRRGate     = autoConfig ? cfg.rrGate     : useRRGate
float effRRMin      = autoConfig ? cfg.rrMinVal   : rrMin

// ── Resolved Compounding Controls ────────────────────────────────────────────
bool  effResetTp    = autoConfig ? cfg.resetTp    : resetTpDaily
float effInitTp     = autoConfig ? cfg.initTp     : initTradeProfit
float effMaxDaily   = autoConfig ? cfg.maxDaily    : maxDailyLoss
int   effMaxConsec  = autoConfig ? cfg.maxConsec   : maxConsecLosses
float effMaxLoss    = autoConfig ? cfg.maxLoss     : maxLossPerTrade
float effFallRatio  = autoConfig ? cfg.fallRatio   : compoundRatio

// ── Resolved Time Windows ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool  effW1En       = autoConfig ? cfg.w1En        : useWin1
float effW1Ratio    = autoConfig ? cfg.w1Ratio     : win1Ratio
bool  effW2En       = autoConfig ? cfg.w2En        : useWin2
float effW2Ratio    = autoConfig ? cfg.w2Ratio     : win2Ratio
bool  effW3En       = autoConfig ? cfg.w3En        : useWin3
float effW3Ratio    = autoConfig ? cfg.w3Ratio     : win3Ratio
bool  effW4En       = autoConfig ? cfg.w4En        : useWin4
float effW4Ratio    = autoConfig ? cfg.w4Ratio     : win4Ratio

// ── Resolved Position Sizing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Enable: checkbox AND per-instrument auto-config flag.
//   useAutoSize=false  → sizing OFF regardless of auto-config (checkbox always wins)
//   useAutoSize=true   → auto-config determines if this instrument has sizing ON
//   autoConfig=false   → useAutoSize alone decides; thresholds from UI inputs
// Thresholds: auto-config ON → per-instrument calibrated UDT values (MYM $50/$50/3, MES $200/$150/5)
//             auto-config OFF → UI inputs (use for calibrating new instruments)
bool  effAutoSize    = useAutoSize and (autoConfig ? cfg.autoSize : true)
float effSizeUpEvery = autoConfig ? cfg.sizeUpEvery   : sizeUpEvery
float effSizeDnEvery = autoConfig ? cfg.sizeDownEvery : sizeDnEvery
int   effSizeMax     = autoConfig ? cfg.sizeMax       : sizeMax

// ── Resolved Day Bias Config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool   effUseApex      = autoConfig ? cfg.useApex     : useApexBias
string effApexMode     = autoConfig ? cfg.apexMode    : apexModeInput
bool   effNeutralTrades = autoConfig ? cfg.neutralBias : neutralTrades

float entryPad = padTicks * syminfo.mintick

// ── Tick Value ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Dollar value of one minimum price movement: mintick x pointvalue.
// Used to convert dollar TP targets into price distances and to
// validate that inputs are achievable on the current instrument.
float tickVal = syminfo.mintick * syminfo.pointvalue

// ── Compounding & Daily Risk State ────────────────────────────────────────────
var float dynamicTp          = 0.0   // compound-adjusted profit target ($)
var float dailyLoss          = 0.0   // cumulative intraday loss — resets daily
var int   consecLosses       = 0     // consecutive losing trades — resets daily
var bool  dailyHalted        = false // no new entries until next session day
var float entryCompoundRatio = 1.0   // ratio captured at entry, used on close
var int   prevClosedCount    = 0
var float entryAtr           = na
var float pivotStopPrice     = na
var bool  beTriggered        = false
var int   lastExit           = na
var float dayPnl             = 0.0   // net P&L for current calendar day (wins + losses)
var float prevDayPnl         = na    // previous day's net P&L — set at day boundary
var int   consecLossDays     = 0     // consecutive days that ended with a net loss
var float sizingCumPnl       = 0.0   // cumulative strategy P&L for contract scaling
var float sizingPeak         = 0.0   // peak of sizingCumPnl — drawdown measured from here

if barstate.isfirst
    dynamicTp          := effInitTp
    entryCompoundRatio := effFallRatio

// ── Daily Reset ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool newDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
if newDay
    // Consecutive loss day tracking: save yesterday's P&L then update streak.
    // Must happen before dayPnl is reset so we capture yesterday's full result.
    prevDayPnl := dayPnl
    if prevDayPnl < 0.0
        consecLossDays := consecLossDays + 1
        // When the consecutive-loss-day halt fires, reset auto-sizing state.
        // Contracts return to the base level so trading resumes conservatively
        // after a sustained drawdown, rather than re-entering at inflated size.
        if effAutoSize and consecLossDays >= maxConsecDays
            sizingCumPnl := 0.0
            sizingPeak   := 0.0
    else
        consecLossDays := 0
    dayPnl       := 0.0
    dailyLoss    := 0.0
    consecLosses := 0
    dailyHalted  := false
    if effResetTp
        dynamicTp := effInitTp

// ── TP Validation & Computation ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// tpTooSmall:  dynamicTp compounded below one tick — target meaningless.
// dlTooNarrow: maxDailyLoss below one tick — any single loss triggers halt.
// tpBelowFloor: TP compounded down below minTpPct of the initial target —
//               entries pause until wins rebuild it back above the floor.
//               This is a temporary trading pause, not a configuration error.
bool  tpTooSmall  = dynamicTp < tickVal
bool  dlTooNarrow = effMaxDaily < tickVal
bool  showWarning = tpTooSmall or dlTooNarrow

float minViableTp  = effInitTp * minTpPct / 100.0
bool  tpBelowFloor = dynamicTp < minViableTp

float effectiveTp   = math.max(dynamicTp, tickVal)           // floor at 1 tick
float tpTicks       = math.ceil(effectiveTp / tickVal)       // ceiling to nearest tick
float tpDist        = tpTicks * syminfo.mintick              // price distance for limit

// Hard per-trade stop: always active regardless of pivot/breakeven settings.
// Converts maxLossPerTrade dollars to a price distance (rounded up to whole ticks).
float hardStopDist  = math.ceil(effMaxLoss / tickVal) * syminfo.mintick

// BE dollar floor: converts beFloorDollars to a price distance (rounded up to ticks).
// Used as an alternative BE trigger when beFloorDollars > 0. The actual trigger
// distance is the minimum of (ATR-based, dollar-floor) — whichever fires first.
float beFloorDist   = beFloorDollars > 0 ? math.ceil(beFloorDollars / tickVal) * syminfo.mintick : na

// ── Session Windows ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Direct hour/minute comparisons — reliable on 24h continuous Globex futures.
// input.session() with TZ overrides silently fails on overnight contracts.
int  barH      = hour(time, TZ)
int  barM      = minute(time, TZ)

// preMarketBlock: hard floor — no entries before PRE_MARKET_FLOOR (07:00 CT).
// Fires regardless of sessionStartHr to guard against NinjaTrader running wider
// session hours than TradingView, which caused pre-market fills in Jun 2026 review.
bool preMarketBlock = barH < PRE_MARKET_FLOOR

bool inSession = barH >= sessionStartHr and barH < sessionEndHr
bool afterLock = barH > entryLockHr or (barH == entryLockHr and barM >= entryLockMin)

// inOpenBlackout: minute-of-day inside the cash-open blackout window (inclusive).
int  barTod        = barH * 60 + barM
int  obStart       = openBlackoutStartHr * 60 + openBlackoutStartMin
int  obEnd         = openBlackoutEndHr   * 60 + openBlackoutEndMin
bool inOpenBlackout = useOpenBlackout and barTod >= obStart and barTod <= obEnd

// isEod: explicit hour:minute pair — independent of sessionEndHr so it can be
// placed before the CME maintenance halt regardless of sessionEndHr setting.
bool isEod     = barH > eodCloseHr or (barH == eodCloseHr and barM >= eodMinute)

// Session open buffer: skip the first N bars after the session gate opens to
// let pre-market swing state settle before accepting entries.
var int  sessionOpenBar   = na
bool     sessionJustOpened = inSession and not inSession[1]
if sessionJustOpened
    sessionOpenBar := bar_index
bool bufferOk      = na(sessionOpenBar) or (bar_index - sessionOpenBar >= sessionOpenBuffer)

// inEntryWindow: pre-market hard block added — always false before 07:00 CT.
// Cash-open blackout also blocks new entries around the 08:30 CT open.
bool inEntryWindow = inSession and not preMarketBlock and not afterLock and not isEod and bufferOk and not inOpenBlackout

// ── Time-of-Day Window Logic ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Uses barH already computed in the Session Windows section above.
// Windows are mutually exclusive and cover the full session.
bool inWin1  = barH >= 7  and barH < 11   // 07:00-11:00 Morning
bool inWin2  = barH >= 11 and barH < 13   // 11:00-13:00 Midday
bool inWin3  = barH >= 13 and barH < 16   // 13:00-16:00 Afternoon
bool inWin4  = barH >= 16                 // 16:00-17:00 Late Day

// windowEnabled: true only when we are inside an enabled time window.
// Used as an entry gate — disabled windows block all new entries.
bool windowEnabled = (inWin1 and effW1En) or (inWin2 and effW2En) or
                     (inWin3 and effW3En) or (inWin4 and effW4En)

// effWindowRatio: the compound ratio for the currently active window.
// Falls back to the global compoundRatio when no window is active.
float effWindowRatio = inWin1 ? effW1Ratio :
                       inWin2 ? effW2Ratio :
                       inWin3 ? effW3Ratio :
                       inWin4 ? effW4Ratio : effFallRatio

// Active window name for status label display.
string winName = inWin1 ? "Morning (07-11)" :
                 inWin2 ? "Midday  (11-13)" :
                 inWin3 ? "Afternoon(13-16)" :
                 inWin4 ? "Late Day(16-17)" : "Off-Hours"

// ── ATR (Wilder RMA, 100-bar) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
float atr = ta.rma(ta.tr(true), 100)

// ── Trend EMA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
float trendEma = ta.ema(close, effEmaLen)
bool  trendUp  = close > trendEma
bool  trendDn  = close < trendEma

plot(drawEma and useTrendFilter ? trendEma : na,
     title = "Trend EMA", color = emaColor, linewidth = 2)

// ── RSI Momentum ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// rsiSlope: RSI change over rsiSlopeLen bars — the "sharpness" measure used by
// both the entry confirmation and the reversal exit. Positive = RSI rising.
float rsiVal   = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
float rsiSlope = rsiVal - rsiVal[rsiSlopeLen]

// ── Bar Classification ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool isUp         = high > high[1] and low > low[1]
bool isDown       = high < high[1] and low < low[1]
bool isMeaningful = isUp or isDown

// ── Swing State ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var SwingState  st     = SwingState.new()
var PivotPoints pivots = PivotPoints.new()

// ── Swing Detection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool swingLow  = isMeaningful and isUp   and st.lastWasDn
bool swingHigh = isMeaningful and isDown and st.lastWasUp

// ── State Update ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if isMeaningful
    st.lastWasUp := isUp
    st.lastWasDn := isDown
    if isUp
        st.upHigh := high
        st.upBar  := bar_index
    if isDown
        st.downLow := low
        st.downBar := bar_index

// ── Filter Evaluation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool trendOkLong  = not useTrendFilter or trendUp
bool trendOkShort = not useTrendFilter or trendDn

float swingLeg    = math.abs(st.upHigh - st.downLow)
bool  sizeOkLong  = not useSwingSize or (not na(swingLeg) and swingLeg >= effSwingSize * atr)
bool  sizeOkShort = sizeOkLong

bool cooldownOk = not useCooldown or na(lastExit) or (bar_index - lastExit >= effCooldown)

// ── RSI Confirmation Gates ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Entry: RSI must be sharply trending in the trade direction (slope past threshold)
// and, optionally, on the bullish/bearish side of the midline.
//   rsiOkLong  — RSI rising hard (and >= midline when the side gate is on)
//   rsiOkShort — RSI falling hard (and <= midline when the side gate is on)
// na(rsiSlope) guard: true (pass) until enough bars exist for the slope lookback.
bool rsiUpSharp   = not na(rsiSlope) and rsiSlope >=  rsiEntrySlope
bool rsiDnSharp   = not na(rsiSlope) and rsiSlope <= -rsiEntrySlope
bool rsiMidOkLong  = not useRsiMid or rsiVal >= rsiMidLevel
bool rsiMidOkShort = not useRsiMid or rsiVal <= rsiMidLevel
bool rsiOkLong    = not useRsiEntry or (na(rsiSlope) ? false : (rsiUpSharp and rsiMidOkLong))
bool rsiOkShort   = not useRsiEntry or (na(rsiSlope) ? false : (rsiDnSharp and rsiMidOkShort))

// Reversal exit: RSI slope flips against the open position beyond the exit threshold.
//   rsiRevDown — sharp down move → exit a LONG
//   rsiRevUp   — sharp up move   → exit a SHORT
bool rsiRevDown = not na(rsiSlope) and rsiSlope <= -rsiExitSlope
bool rsiRevUp   = not na(rsiSlope) and rsiSlope >=  rsiExitSlope

// ── Apex Adaptive Trend (Embedded) ────────────────────────────────────────────
// Adapted from "Apex Adaptive Trend Navigator [Pineify]" (MPL 2.0 © Pineify).
// Efficiency = |net price move over N bars| / |sum of all bar-to-bar moves|
// — a KAMA-style adaptive factor.  apexTrendDir: price vs adaptive MA.
// apexStructDir: Break-of-Structure via higher swing highs / lower swing lows.
string apexTicker   = str.length(apexSymbolInput) > 0 ? apexSymbolInput : syminfo.tickerid
string apexTf       = str.length(effApexTfInput) > 0 ? effApexTfInput : timeframe.period
[apexSrc, apexHi, apexLo] = request.security(apexTicker, apexTf, [close, high, low], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

float apexPriceChg  = apexSrc - apexSrc[effApexPeriod]
float apexAbsChg    = math.abs(apexPriceChg)
float apexSumChg    = math.sum(math.abs(apexSrc - apexSrc[1]), effApexPeriod)
float apexEff       = apexSumChg > 0 ? apexAbsChg / apexSumChg : 0.0
var float apexMa    = na
apexMa             := nz(apexMa[1], apexSrc) + math.pow(apexEff, 2) * (apexSrc - nz(apexMa[1], apexSrc))
int apexTrendDir    = apexSrc > apexMa ? 1 : -1

float apexPivHi     = ta.pivothigh(apexHi, effApexPeriod, effApexPeriod)
float apexPivLo     = ta.pivotlow(apexLo,  effApexPeriod, effApexPeriod)
var float apexLastHi = na
var float apexLastLo = na
var int   apexStructDir = 0

if not na(apexPivHi)
    float newHi = apexHi[apexLen]
    if not na(apexLastHi)
        apexStructDir := newHi > apexLastHi ? 1 : -1
    apexLastHi := newHi

if not na(apexPivLo)
    float newLo = apexLo[apexLen]
    if not na(apexLastLo)
        apexStructDir := newLo < apexLastLo ? -1 : 1
    apexLastLo := newLo

// ── Day Bias Resolution ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Manual path: fuzzy keyword match — empty text falls back to tradeDir.
bool   mbIsBull    = str.contains(str.lower(manualBiasText), "bull")
bool   mbIsBear    = str.contains(str.lower(manualBiasText), "bear")
bool   mbIsNeut    = str.contains(str.lower(manualBiasText), "neutral") or str.contains(str.lower(manualBiasText), "both")
bool   mbHasSignal = mbIsBull or mbIsBear or mbIsNeut
string manualBias  = mbHasSignal ? (mbIsBull ? "Bullish" : mbIsBear ? "Bearish" : "Neutral") : "UseTradeDir"

// Apex path: derive from embedded calculations according to selected mode.
bool apexTrendBull  = apexTrendDir  ==  1
bool apexTrendBear  = apexTrendDir  == -1
bool apexStructBull = apexStructDir ==  1
bool apexStructBear = apexStructDir == -1
bool apexBull = effApexMode == "Structure (BOS/CHoCH)" ? apexStructBull : effApexMode == "Both Agree" ? (apexTrendBull and apexStructBull) : apexTrendBull
bool apexBear = effApexMode == "Structure (BOS/CHoCH)" ? apexStructBear : effApexMode == "Both Agree" ? (apexTrendBear and apexStructBear) : apexTrendBear
string apexBias = apexBull ? "Bullish" : apexBear ? "Bearish" : "Neutral"

// effectiveBias: Apex wins when ON, else manual, else UseTradeDir.
string effectiveBias = effUseApex ? apexBias : manualBias

// biasAllowLong/Short: the final entry direction gate.
//   UseTradeDir → respect the Trade Direction dropdown as normal.
//   Neutral     → allow both if effNeutralTrades=ON, block all if OFF.
//   Bullish/Bearish → override Trade Direction entirely.
// effNeutralTrades: resolved from auto-config (per-instrument) or manual input.
// MES auto-config locks this OFF — when Apex is neutral/unclear, no entries fire.
bool biasIsNeutral  = effectiveBias == "Neutral"
bool biasAllowLong  = effectiveBias == "UseTradeDir" ? (tradeDir != "Short Only") : (effectiveBias == "Bullish" or (biasIsNeutral and effNeutralTrades))
bool biasAllowShort = effectiveBias == "UseTradeDir" ? (tradeDir != "Long Only")  : (effectiveBias == "Bearish" or (biasIsNeutral and effNeutralTrades))

// Status label display strings.
string apexSymDisp  = str.length(apexSymbolInput) > 0 ? apexSymbolInput : syminfo.root
string apexArrow    = apexTrendDir == 1 ? "↑" : "↓"
string biasTag      = effUseApex ? " (Apex:" + apexSymDisp + " " + apexArrow + ")" : mbHasSignal ? " (manual)" : " (tradeDir)"
string biasDisplay  = effectiveBias + biasTag

// ── R:R Gate ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Stop distance uses the actual pivot level when Pivot Stop is ON.
// Falls back to 1x ATR when Pivot Stop is OFF (no explicit stop defined).
// tpDist / stopDist must meet rrMin to allow entry.
float longStopLevel  = st.downLow - effPivotBuf * atr
float longStopDist   = effPivotStop ? math.max(close - longStopLevel, syminfo.mintick) : atr
float longRR         = tpDist / longStopDist
bool  rrOkLong       = not effRRGate or longRR >= effRRMin

float shortStopLevel = st.upHigh + effPivotBuf * atr
float shortStopDist  = effPivotStop ? math.max(shortStopLevel - close, syminfo.mintick) : atr
float shortRR        = tpDist / shortStopDist
bool  rrOkShort      = not effRRGate or shortRR >= effRRMin

// ── Entry Gate ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Entries blocked when:
//   dailyHalted      — max daily loss or consecutive loss limit reached
//   consecDayHalted  — too many consecutive calendar days ended with a net loss
//   showWarning      — TP or daily loss target below one tick
//   not windowEnabled   — current time is outside all enabled windows
//   not rrOkLong/Short  — R:R below minimum threshold for this direction
//   not biasAllowLong/Short — day bias blocks this direction
// biasAllow already incorporates tradeDir as a fallback — no separate check needed.
// tpBelowFloor pauses entries when compounding has driven the TP below the
// minimum viable threshold — entries resume automatically when TP recovers.
bool consecDayHalted = consecLossDays >= maxConsecDays

// ── Auto Position Sizing — contract count ─────────────────────────────────────
// sizeExtra: floor(cumProfit / upEvery) - floor(drawdown / dnEvery), clamped 0..sizeMax.
// Uses cumulative net P&L from all closed trades since strategy start.
// Drawdown is measured from the running peak of that cumulative P&L.
// Updated one bar after each trade close (var state carries forward).
float sizingDrawdown = math.max(0.0, sizingPeak - sizingCumPnl)
int   sizeExtra      = effAutoSize ? math.max(0, math.min(effSizeMax,
     int(math.floor(math.max(0.0, sizingCumPnl) / effSizeUpEvery)) -
     int(math.floor(sizingDrawdown / effSizeDnEvery)))) : 0
int   effContracts   = contracts + sizeExtra

bool goLong  = swingLow  and inEntryWindow and cooldownOk and trendOkLong  and sizeOkLong
               and biasAllowLong and rsiOkLong
               and not dailyHalted and not consecDayHalted and not showWarning and not tpBelowFloor
               and windowEnabled and rrOkLong

bool goShort = swingHigh and inEntryWindow and cooldownOk and trendOkShort and sizeOkShort
               and biasAllowShort and rsiOkShort
               and not dailyHalted and not consecDayHalted and not showWarning and not tpBelowFloor
               and windowEnabled and rrOkShort

// ── Entries ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Stop price helpers: compute the active stop level at entry time so it can be
// embedded in the alert JSON. TradersPost forwards stopPrice to NinjaTrader,
// which places a native bracket stop at fill — independent of TV webhook delivery.
//
// Long stop:  highest of (pivot − buffer, hard stop).  Pivot wins when nearby.
// Short stop: lowest  of (pivot + buffer, hard stop).  Pivot wins when nearby.
//
// Uses close as entry price proxy (market order). Actual fill may differ by 1–2
// ticks in fast markets — the hard stop distance absorbs this safely.

if goLong
    entryAtr           := atr
    beTriggered        := false
    pivotStopPrice     := st.downLow
    entryCompoundRatio := effWindowRatio   // capture window ratio at entry time
    strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty = effContracts, comment = "SwingLow")
    // Compute stop price for native broker bracket order
    float lHardStop  = close - hardStopDist
    float lPivStop   = effPivotStop ? st.downLow - effPivotBuf * atr : lHardStop
    float lStopPrice = math.max(lHardStop, lPivStop)
    string bTicker   = syminfo.ticker
    string bQty      = str.tostring(effContracts)
    string bStop     = str.tostring(lStopPrice, format.mintick)
    string buyMsg    = useMarketOrders ?
         '{"ticker":"' + bTicker + '","action":"buy","sentiment":"bullish","quantity":' + bQty + ',"stopPrice":"' + bStop + '"}' :
         '{"ticker":"' + bTicker + '","action":"buy","sentiment":"bullish","price":"' + str.tostring(close + entryPad, format.mintick) + '","quantity":' + bQty + ',"stopPrice":"' + bStop + '"}'
    alert(buyMsg, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

if goShort
    entryAtr           := atr
    beTriggered        := false
    pivotStopPrice     := st.upHigh
    entryCompoundRatio := effWindowRatio   // capture window ratio at entry time
    strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty = effContracts, comment = "SwingHigh")
    // Compute stop price for native broker bracket order
    float sHardStop  = close + hardStopDist
    float sPivStop   = effPivotStop ? st.upHigh + effPivotBuf * atr : sHardStop
    float sStopPrice = math.min(sHardStop, sPivStop)
    string sTicker   = syminfo.ticker
    string sQty      = str.tostring(effContracts)
    string sStop     = str.tostring(sStopPrice, format.mintick)
    string sellMsg   = useMarketOrders ?
         '{"ticker":"' + sTicker + '","action":"sell","sentiment":"bearish","quantity":' + sQty + ',"stopPrice":"' + sStop + '"}' :
         '{"ticker":"' + sTicker + '","action":"sell","sentiment":"bearish","price":"' + str.tostring(close - entryPad, format.mintick) + '","quantity":' + sQty + ',"stopPrice":"' + sStop + '"}'
    alert(sellMsg, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ── Auto Breakeven Check ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if effBreakeven and not beTriggered and not na(entryAtr)
    // beTrigDist: the smaller of the ATR-based trigger and the dollar floor.
    // Whichever is closer to entry fires first. When beFloorDollars = 0 the
    // floor is na so we fall back to the ATR-only distance.
    float atrBeDist  = effBeTrigger * entryAtr
    float beTrigDist = na(beFloorDist) ? atrBeDist : math.min(atrBeDist, beFloorDist)
    if strategy.position_size > 0
        if high >= strategy.position_avg_price + beTrigDist
            beTriggered := true
    if strategy.position_size < 0
        if low <= strategy.position_avg_price - beTrigDist
            beTriggered := true

// ── Exit Orders — TP limit + stop (OCO) ──────────────────────────────────────
// strategy.exit submits a limit (TP) and stop simultaneously.
// Whichever fills first cancels the other.
// Re-submitted each bar so tpDist stays current if dynamicTp changes.
//
// Stop hierarchy (most protective wins):
//   hardStop — always present; dollar-based floor via maxLossPerTrade
//   pivStop  — optional pivot level; tighter than hardStop when pivot is nearby
//   beStop   — overrides both after breakeven trigger; locks in small profit
//
// For longs: stop triggers when price FALLS to the level → take the HIGHEST
//   (most protective = closest to entry from below)
// For shorts: stop triggers when price RISES to the level → take the LOWEST
//   (most protective = closest to entry from above, or below entry after BE)
if strategy.position_size > 0 and not na(entryAtr)
    float tpLimit  = strategy.position_avg_price + tpDist
    float hardStop = strategy.position_avg_price - hardStopDist
    float pivStop  = effPivotStop ? pivotStopPrice - effPivotBuf * entryAtr : na
    float beStop   = effBreakeven ? strategy.position_avg_price + effBeBuf * entryAtr : na
    float baseStop = beTriggered  ? beStop : pivStop
    // math.max: for longs, higher stop = more protective (triggers sooner on reversal)
    float actStop  = na(baseStop) ? hardStop : math.max(hardStop, baseStop)
    string lossLbl = beTriggered ? "BE Stop" : effPivotStop ? "Pivot Stop" : "Hard Stop"
    strategy.exit("Long Exit", from_entry = "Long",
        limit          = tpLimit,
        stop           = actStop,
        comment_profit = "TP Hit",
        comment_loss   = lossLbl)

if strategy.position_size < 0 and not na(entryAtr)
    float tpLimit  = strategy.position_avg_price - tpDist
    float hardStop = strategy.position_avg_price + hardStopDist
    float pivStop  = effPivotStop ? pivotStopPrice + effPivotBuf * entryAtr : na
    float beStop   = effBreakeven ? strategy.position_avg_price - effBeBuf * entryAtr : na
    float baseStop = beTriggered  ? beStop : pivStop
    // math.min: for shorts, lower stop = more protective (triggers sooner on reversal)
    float actStop  = na(baseStop) ? hardStop : math.min(hardStop, baseStop)
    string sLossLbl = beTriggered ? "BE Stop" : effPivotStop ? "Pivot Stop" : "Hard Stop"
    strategy.exit("Short Exit", from_entry = "Short",
        limit          = tpLimit,
        stop           = actStop,
        comment_profit = "TP Hit",
        comment_loss   = sLossLbl)

// ── RSI Reversal Exit (OR with TP / stop / EOD) ───────────────────────────────
// Closes the position at market when RSI momentum flips against it beyond the
// reversal threshold. strategy.close() emits a market order; the resulting trade
// close is picked up by the trade-close detection block below (compounding update
// + {"action":"exit"} alert), exactly like a TP/stop/EOD exit. The entry required
// RSI sharply WITH the trade, so a reversal cannot fire on the entry bar itself.
if useRsiExit and strategy.position_size > 0 and rsiRevDown
    strategy.close("Long",  comment = "RSI Reversal")
if useRsiExit and strategy.position_size < 0 and rsiRevUp
    strategy.close("Short", comment = "RSI Reversal")

// ── EOD Force-Close ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if isEod and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD Close")
    lastExit := bar_index

// ── Trade Close Detection — compounding + daily risk + alerts ─────────────────
// Fires on every close type: TP hit, stop, reversal, EOD.
// Uses entryCompoundRatio (captured at entry) — not the current window ratio —
// so a morning trade compounds at the morning rate even if it closes at noon.
string exitMsg = '{"ticker":"' + syminfo.ticker + '","action":"exit"}'

if strategy.closedtrades > prevClosedCount
    float lastProfit = strategy.closedtrades.profit(strategy.closedtrades - 1)
    dayPnl       := dayPnl + lastProfit   // accumulate net for consecutive-day tracking
    sizingCumPnl := sizingCumPnl + lastProfit
    if sizingCumPnl > sizingPeak
        sizingPeak := sizingCumPnl
    if lastProfit >= 0
        // Win: grow TP target by entry-time ratio, reset consecutive loss count
        consecLosses := 0
        dynamicTp    := dynamicTp * entryCompoundRatio
    else
        // Loss: shrink TP (floor 1 tick), accumulate daily loss, check halt conditions
        consecLosses := consecLosses + 1
        dailyLoss    := dailyLoss + math.abs(lastProfit)
        dynamicTp    := math.max(dynamicTp / entryCompoundRatio, tickVal)
        if dailyLoss >= effMaxDaily or consecLosses >= effMaxConsec
            dailyHalted := true
    lastExit        := bar_index
    prevClosedCount := strategy.closedtrades
    alert(exitMsg, alert.freq_once_per_bar)

// ── Arrows ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plotshape(goLong  and drawArrows, title = "Buy Signal",
          style = shape.arrowup,   location = location.belowbar,
          color = upColor, size = size.small)
plotshape(goShort and drawArrows, title = "Sell Signal",
          style = shape.arrowdown, location = location.abovebar,
          color = dnColor, size = size.small)

// ── Swing Lines ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if swingHigh and drawLines
    chart.point hp = chart.point.from_index(st.upBar, st.upHigh)
    if not na(pivots.low)
        line.new(pivots.low, hp, color = lineColor, width = lineWt)
    pivots.high := hp

if swingLow and drawLines
    chart.point lp = chart.point.from_index(st.downBar, st.downLow)
    if not na(pivots.high)
        line.new(pivots.high, lp, color = lineColor, width = lineWt)
    pivots.low := lp

// ── Pre-Market Warning Label ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Orange label when the chart's current bar is inside the pre-market hard block.
// Reminds you that NinjaTrader must also have session hours set to 07:00+ CT
// so it matches TradingView and doesn't execute alerts from earlier bars.
var label preMarketLabel = na
if barstate.islast and preMarketBlock
    if not na(preMarketLabel)
        label.delete(preMarketLabel)
    preMarketLabel := label.new(
         x         = bar_index,
         y         = high,
         text      = "PRE-MARKET BLOCK ACTIVE — entries suppressed before " + str.tostring(PRE_MARKET_FLOOR) + ":00 CT\nVerify NinjaTrader session start = 07:00 CT (08:00 ET)",
         xloc      = xloc.bar_index,
         yloc      = yloc.abovebar,
         style     = label.style_label_down,
         color     = color.orange,
         textcolor = color.black,
         size      = size.normal)

// ── Warning Label — tick size mismatch ───────────────────────────────────────
// Fires when any dollar input cannot be expressed as at least one full tick.
// Trading is blocked until the mismatch is resolved.
var label warnLabel = na
if barstate.islast and showWarning
    if not na(warnLabel)
        label.delete(warnLabel)
    string wA = "PARAMETER MISMATCH — ENTRIES BLOCKED"
    string wB = tpTooSmall  ? "TP $" + str.tostring(dynamicTp, "#.##") + " < 1 tick ($" + str.tostring(tickVal, "#.##") + ") — raise Initial Trade Profit Target" : ""
    string wC = dlTooNarrow ? "Daily Loss $" + str.tostring(effMaxDaily, "#.##") + " < 1 tick ($" + str.tostring(tickVal, "#.##") + ") — raise Max Daily Loss" : ""
    string wD = syminfo.ticker + " tick = $" + str.tostring(tickVal, "#.##")
    warnLabel := label.new(
         x         = bar_index,
         y         = high,
         text      = wA + "\n" + wB + "\n" + wC + "\n" + wD,
         xloc      = xloc.bar_index,
         yloc      = yloc.abovebar,
         style     = label.style_label_down,
         color     = color.red,
         textcolor = color.white,
         size      = size.normal)

// ── Status Label ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Right-edge label showing compounding state, daily risk, window, and R:R.
// Background turns red when trading is halted for the day.
var label statusLabel = na
if barstate.islast and showStatus
    if not na(statusLabel)
        label.delete(statusLabel)
    string haltStr  = consecDayHalted ? " [DAY STREAK HALT " + str.tostring(consecLossDays) + "d]" : dailyHalted ? " [HALTED]" : tpBelowFloor ? " [TP FLOOR]" : inOpenBlackout ? " [OPEN BLACKOUT]" : (not windowEnabled ? " [WINDOW OFF]" : "")
    string winStr   = windowEnabled ? winName + "  x" + str.tostring(effWindowRatio, "#.##") : winName + " (disabled)"
    string rrLStr   = "Long  R:R: " + str.tostring(longRR,  "#.##") + (rrOkLong  ? "" : " [below min]")
    string rrSStr   = "Short R:R: " + str.tostring(shortRR, "#.##") + (rrOkShort ? "" : " [below min]")
    string ln1      = "Compounding Machine: " + syminfo.root + haltStr
    string ln2      = "Day Bias     : " + biasDisplay
    string ln3      = "TP Target    : $" + str.tostring(dynamicTp, "#.##") + " (" + str.tostring(tpTicks, "#") + " ticks)  floor=$" + str.tostring(minViableTp, "#.##") + (tpBelowFloor ? " ◄ PAUSED" : "")
    string ln4      = "Daily Loss   : $" + str.tostring(dailyLoss, "#.##") + " / $" + str.tostring(effMaxDaily, "#.##")
    string ln5      = "Consec Losses: " + str.tostring(consecLosses) + " / " + str.tostring(effMaxConsec) + "   Loss Days: " + str.tostring(consecLossDays) + " / " + str.tostring(maxConsecDays) + (consecDayHalted ? " ◄ HALTED" : "")
    string ln6      = "Window       : " + winStr
    string ln7      = rrLStr + "   " + rrSStr
    string rsiState = na(rsiSlope) ? "warming up" :
                      rsiUpSharp ? "sharp ↑" : rsiDnSharp ? "sharp ↓" : "flat"
    string rsiGate  = not useRsiEntry ? "OFF" :
                      (rsiOkLong and rsiOkShort) ? "both ok" :
                      rsiOkLong ? "long ok" : rsiOkShort ? "short ok" : "blocked"
    string rsiExitS = useRsiExit ? ("  exit@±" + str.tostring(rsiExitSlope, "#.#")) : "  exit OFF"
    string rsiSlopeStr = na(rsiSlope) ? "na" : (rsiSlope >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(rsiSlope, "#.#")
    string ln7b     = "RSI(" + str.tostring(rsiLen) + ") : " + str.tostring(rsiVal, "#.#") +
                      "  slope " + rsiSlopeStr + "/" + str.tostring(rsiSlopeLen) + "b (" + rsiState + ")" +
                      "  entry[" + rsiGate + "]" + rsiExitS
    string sizingStr = effAutoSize ?
         "ON  contracts=" + str.tostring(effContracts) + " (base " + str.tostring(contracts) + " +" + str.tostring(sizeExtra) + " extra)" +
         "  cumPnl=$" + str.tostring(sizingCumPnl, "#.##") +
         "  peak=$"   + str.tostring(sizingPeak,   "#.##") +
         "  DD=$"     + str.tostring(sizingDrawdown, "#.##") :
         "OFF  (fixed " + str.tostring(contracts) + " contract" + (contracts > 1 ? "s)" : ")")
    string ln8      = "Sizing       : " + sizingStr
    string apexCfgStr = effUseApex ? " | Apex:" + effApexMode + " len=" + str.tostring(effApexPeriod) + " tf=" + effApexTfInput : ""
    string autoStr  = autoConfig ? "ON (" + str.tostring(effSwingSize, "#.#") + "x ATR, EMA " + str.tostring(effEmaLen) + ", initTP=$" + str.tostring(effInitTp, "#") + ", maxLoss=$" + str.tostring(effMaxLoss, "#") + apexCfgStr + ")" : "OFF"
    string ln9      = "Auto-Config  : " + autoStr
    color lblColor  = (dailyHalted or consecDayHalted) ? color.new(color.red, 20) :
                      tpBelowFloor ? color.new(color.purple, 20) :
                      not windowEnabled ? color.new(color.orange, 20) :
                      effectiveBias == "Bullish" ? color.new(color.green, 30) :
                      effectiveBias == "Bearish" ? color.new(color.maroon, 20) :
                      color.new(color.navy, 20)
    statusLabel := label.new(
         x         = bar_index,
         y         = high,
         text      = ln1 + "\n" + ln2 + "\n" + ln3 + "\n" + ln4 + "\n" + ln5 + "\n" + ln6 + "\n" + ln7 + "\n" + ln7b + "\n" + ln8 + "\n" + ln9,
         xloc      = xloc.bar_index,
         yloc      = yloc.abovebar,
         style     = label.style_label_left,
         color     = lblColor,
         textcolor = color.white,
         size      = size.small)

// ── TradersPost Alert Setup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// TRADINGVIEW ALERT SETUP:
//   1. Click the clock icon -> Create Alert
//   2. Condition: "Futures Compounding Machine" -> "Any alert() function call"
//   3. Webhook URL: paste your TradersPost webhook URL
//   4. Message body: leave blank — the script sends full JSON automatically
//   5. Set expiry as far out as TradingView allows
//
// JSON sent per event (Market Orders ON):
//   BUY  entry -> {"action":"buy",  "sentiment":"bullish","quantity":N,"stopPrice":"P"}
//   SELL entry -> {"action":"sell", "sentiment":"bearish","quantity":N,"stopPrice":"P"}
//   EXIT       -> {"action":"exit"}   (fires on TP hit, stop, reversal, or EOD)
//
// stopPrice is the computed stop level (pivot or hard stop, whichever is tighter).
// TradersPost forwards this to NinjaTrader, which places a native bracket stop at
// fill time — the position is protected even if subsequent TV webhooks are delayed.
//
// NINJATRADER SESSION HOURS — MUST MATCH TRADINGVIEW:
//   Set NinjaTrader strategy session start to 07:00 CT (08:00 ET) minimum.
//   Pre-market fills were observed in Jun 2026 when NT ran wider hours than TV.
//   The Pine hard floor (PRE_MARKET_FLOOR = 07:00 CT) suppresses TV signals, but
//   NT must also be configured to ignore any alerts that arrive before 07:00 CT.
//
// EXIT ALERT NOTE:
//   The exit alert remains a flat market close. The native bracket stop placed at
//   entry handles emergency protection. The TV exit alert fires on TP hit or EOD
//   and serves as a confirmation close — it is no longer the primary stop mechanism.
